led("BTHREE-C13",21,"In spring in the Valley of Sweet-chestnuts Ralph kills a huge bear that chased Ursula after she bathed in the river. They declare their love; Ursula wishes to wait for the yearly messengers of the Innocent Folk as wedding witnesses. Ralph skins the bear.","Rock-house with toft and quicken-tree; chestnut grove between it and the river; meadow sloping to river; sandy bight under the mountains; bear carcase two furlongs from the dwelling.",["Exact layout of the valley relative to the mountains."])
led("BTHREE-C14",11,"Messengers of the Innocent Folk (an elder and two young men with oxen) arrive and offer to guide them to the House of the Sorceress. They build a wattled bower in the chestnut grove and witness Ralph and Ursula's wedding that night.","Bower in chestnut grove; messengers come yearly to the cave.",[])
led("BTHREE-C15",7,"Travelling with the messengers, the couple leave the mountains in three days, see them as a cloud after six, meet shepherds on day eight and on day nine enter a settled valley and the unfenced town of the Innocent Folk, where they are feasted in the Temple/Mote-house/Guest-house.","Route: Valley of Sweet-chestnuts -> out of mountains (3 days) -> mountains a cloud behind (6 days) -> sheep on green hillside (8 days) -> wide valley and town (9th day). No compass direction given.",["Direction from the mountains to the Innocent Folk."])
